{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Your eye shall not spare him</b> — that you should not say: the first one has already been killed; why are we killing this one, so that two dead are found? This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 19:13), from Sifrei (Sifrei 187). But the correct reasoning for \"you shall not say\" is: just as we spare the blood of the slain, so it is fitting that we spare the blood of the living.\n\nBut the correct interpretation is that Scripture commands concerning those liable to capital punishments: \"and you shall purge the evil from your midst\" — and that is a positive commandment. But because of the proliferation of stumbling-blocks, it further warns with a negative commandment, that they should not escape from our hands — neither out of fear of them nor because compassion is granted to them. Thus Scripture mentions the same regarding the inciter (Deuteronomy 13:9), and says \"You shall not allow a sorceress to live\" (Exodus 22:17), because she causes great turmoil, selling many through her sorcery; and \"you shall cut off her hand — your eye shall not spare\" (Deuteronomy 25:12), because the simpletons will praise her when she helps her husband, or because shame is common and involves no monetary loss; and likewise with conspiring witnesses Scripture commands (Deuteronomy 19:21) that they not be shown compassion, because nothing was actually done through their testimony, or because their stumbling-block is great." "And the reason for <b>and it shall be good for you</b> is that purging innocent blood is a commandment and a great benefit to you, to deliver your soul from death — for showing compassion to murderers is tantamount to shedding blood, at the hands of the murderers and at the hands of others who are emboldened."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase כַּאֲשֶׁר נָחוּס עַל דַּם הֶהָרוּג טוֹב שֶׁנָּחוּס עַל דַּם הַחַי is rendered hyper-literally; Ramban here seems to present an alternative rationale before giving his own view with וְהַנָּכוֹן."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:51.678741323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}